' Builds every fission/tests/*.abas smoke fixture as its own cached Rivet ArcoCapsule target,
' instead of leaving them to be invoked via `ArcoFission compile-run` from source.
'
' The problem this fixes: `ArcoFission compile-run FILE.abas` re-lexes/re-parses/re-lowers the
' ENTIRE shared Fission frontend (fission/core, fission/sir, fission/language/arcobasic -- several
' thousand lines of ArcoBASIC) from source on every single invocation, because compile-run always
' compiles fresh. tests/integration/fission_substrate_core_smoke.sh calls compile-run once per
' fixture -- 50 separate processes, 50 separate from-source recompiles of the same shared frontend,
' every single run, whether or not anything changed. That is the dominant cost in `fissure run
' --full` (observed: 363s for what is otherwise a small amount of real test-body work).
'
' The fix is the same "build once, reuse" pattern already proven for language.arcobasic's own
' executable module in rivet_modules.abas: each fixture becomes a real Rivet Compile action with
' proper fingerprinting (via ArcoCapsuleTarget's now-fixed transitive #IMPORT closure -- see
' rivet/stdlib/rivet.abas), so `rivet build` only recompiles a fixture when its own source or
' anything it imports actually changed, and running the prebuilt capsule directly pays only VM
' startup + the fixture's own tiny test body -- no frontend recompilation at all.
'
' `ArcoFission build` and `ArcoFission compile-run` both execute on the same bytecode VM (see
' `ArcoFission --help`: compile-run and the default `build` both target the ELF64/bytecode-VM
' path), so a prebuilt capsule's stdout is expected to be byte-identical to compile-run's -- this
' is a build/dispatch change only, not a behavior change, and the integration smoke script's exact
' golden-output greps should not need to change.

#IMPORT "fission/build/rivet_modules.abas"

FUNCTION Fission_RivetTestBaseName(entryPath)
    segments = String.Split(entryPath, "/")
    last = segments[LEN(segments) - 1]
    RETURN String.Slice(last, 0, String.Length(last) - String.Length(".abas"))
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Fission_RivetTestEntries()
    entries = []
    FOR entry IN DIRECTORY("fission/tests", FALSE)
        IF entry.Extension == ".abas" THEN ignored = Array.Push(entries, entry.Path)
    NEXT
    RETURN entries
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Fission_RivetBuildTestCapsule(entryPath, compilerTarget)
    target = BUILD.ArcoCapsule(Fission_RivetTestBaseName(entryPath))
    target.Entry = entryPath
    target.OutputDirectory = "build-rivet/fission/tests"
    ignored = target.UseCompilerTarget(compilerTarget)
    ignored = target.Build()
    RETURN target
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Fission_RivetBuildAllTestCapsules(compilerTarget)
    targets = []
    FOR entryPath IN Fission_RivetTestEntries()
        ignored = Array.Push(targets, Fission_RivetBuildTestCapsule(entryPath, compilerTarget))
    NEXT
    RETURN targets
END FUNCTION
